{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791040580,"nonce":"S2LZg/3/vVYM2T9k5mzAhheyDvA=","message":"b79dee9: records are no longer vertex inputs. The renderer uploads the display list into an rgba32float texture (RecordLayout: 16 rows a record, 2048 texels wide, 128 records a row), bound alone in group 1, and UiFramework's transform rewrites each primitive.field into a textureLoad of that row at instanceID, carried to the fragment stage as one flat i32 varying. One shader source for every platform, including those without storage buffers (WebGL2, older GLES), where Blinc keeps three hand-written copies (storage, _vb, _dt). Varyings for BoxShader went from about 15 to 3; the record can now grow past 16 rows by raising RECORD_ROWS (whole records per 2048-texel row). Frame times unchanged on the Mac and the NUC (60 fps, ui 0.2-0.3 ms, encode+submit 0.3-0.4 ms). Downlevel devices still cannot be created through hlwgpu (requestDevice requests at least WebGPU's default limits); asked hlwgpu-9f.","files":null}]}